        "edanEntry": "{\"id\":\"edanmdm-npg_NPG.71.24\",\"title\":\"Abraham Lincoln\",\"unitCode\":\"NPG\",\"linkedId\":\"0\",\"type\":\"edanmdm\",\"url\":\"edanmdm:npg_NPG.71.24\",\"content\":{\"descriptiveNonRepeating\":{\"record_ID\":\"npg_NPG.71.24\",\"online_media\":{\"mediaCount\":\"1\",\"media\":[{\"thumbnail\":\"http://ids.si.edu/ids/deliveryService?id=NPG-NPG_71_24Lincolnv1_d1\",\"idsId\":\"NPG-NPG_71_24Lincolnv1_d1\",\"usage\":{\"access\":\"Usage conditions apply\",\"text\":\"\"},\"type\":\"Images\",\"content\":\"http://ids.si.edu/ids/deliveryService?id=NPG-NPG_71_24Lincolnv1_d1\"}]},\"unit_code\":\"NPG\",\"title_sort\":\"ABRAHAM LINCOLN\",\"record_link\":\"http://npg.si.edu/object/npg_NPG.71.24\",\"title\":{\"label\":\"Title\",\"content\":\"Abraham Lincoln\"},\"metadata_usage\":{\"access\":\"Usage conditions apply\",\"text\":\"\"},\"data_source\":\"National Portrait Gallery\"},\"indexedStructured\":{\"date\":[\"1860s\"],\"exhibition\":[{\"exhibitionTitle\":\"America's Presidents (Reinstallation September 2017)\",\"building\":\"NPG\",\"room\":\"South Gallery 240\"}],\"object_type\":[\"Sculpture (visual work)\"],\"geoLocation\":[{\"L1\":{\"type\":\"Continent\",\"content\":\" North America\"},\"L2\":{\"type\":\"Country\",\"content\":\"United States of America\"}},{\"L1\":{\"type\":\"Continent\",\"content\":\" North America\"},\"L2\":{\"type\":\"Country\",\"content\":\"United States of America\"}},{\"L1\":{\"type\":\"Continent\",\"content\":\" North America\"},\"L2\":{\"type\":\"Country\",\"content\":\"United States of America\"},\"L3\":{\"type\":\"State\",\"content\":\"Illinois\"}},{\"L1\":{\"type\":\"Continent\",\"content\":\" North America\"},\"L2\":{\"type\":\"Country\",\"content\":\"United States of America\"}}],\"name\":[\"Lincoln, Abraham\",\"Volk, Leonard Wells\"],\"onPhysicalExhibit\":[\"Yes\"],\"topic\":[\"Business and Finance\",\"Legislators\",\"Soldiers\",\"Merchants\",\"Businessperson\",\"Life mask\",\"Masks\",\"Reformers\",\"Crafts and Trades\",\"Public officers\",\"Presidents\",\"Military\",\"Activism\",\"Congressmen\",\"Government\",\"Society and social change\",\"Portraits\",\"Lawyers\",\"Ecology\",\"Boat builder\",\"Law and Law Enforcement\",\"Surveyors\",\"Men\",\"Senators\",\"Politics\",\"Postmasters\"],\"place\":[\"United States\",\"Illinois\"],\"online_media_type\":[\"Images\"]},\"freetext\":{\"setName\":[{\"label\":\"See more items in\",\"content\":\"National Portrait Gallery Collection\"},{\"label\":\"Exhibition\",\"content\":\"America's Presidents (Reinstallation September 2017)\"},{\"label\":\"On View\",\"content\":\"NPG, South Gallery 240\"}],\"date\":[{\"label\":\"Date\",\"content\":\"1917 cast after 1860 original\"}],\"identifier\":[{\"label\":\"Object number\",\"content\":\"NPG.71.24\"}],\"notes\":[{\"label\":\"Exhibition Label\",\"content\":\"Born Hardin County, Kentucky\"},{\"label\":\"Exhibition Label\",\"content\":\"Leonard Wells Volk made this life mask of Abraham Lincoln in 1860, before Lincoln began his run for the\"},{\"label\":\"Exhibition Label\",\"content\":\"presidency. Volk had wanted to create a bust of him to add to his collection of American statesmen, but Lincoln did not have time to pose. Poet and editor Richard Watson Gilder, who owned a bronze version of the work, wrote after Lincoln’s assassination, “This bronze doth keep the very form and mold / Of our great martyr’s face. Yes, this is he: / That brow all wisdom and benignity . . . .”\"},{\"label\":\"Exhibition Label\",\"content\":\"Nacido en el condado de Hardin, Kentucky\"},{\"label\":\"Exhibition Label\",\"content\":\"Leonard Wells Volk tomó este molde de la cara de Lincoln en 1860, antes de que este se postulara para\"},{\"label\":\"Exhibition Label\",\"content\":\"la presidencia. Volk quería crear un busto de él para añadirlo a su colección de estadistas estadounidenses, pero Lincoln no tenía tiempo para posar. El poeta y editor Richard Watson Gilder, quien poseía una version de la obra en bronce, escribió después del asesinato de\"},{\"label\":\"Exhibition Label\",\"content\":\"Lincoln: “Este bronce en verdad conserva las formas del rostro de nuestro gran mártir. Sí, es él: esa frente que es toda sabiduría y bondad . . .”.\"},{\"label\":\"Provenance\",\"content\":\"National Museum of American History (now National Museum of American History); transferred to NPG 1971\"}],\"creditLine\":[{\"label\":\"Credit Line\",\"content\":\"National Portrait Gallery, Smithsonian Institution; transfer from the National Museum of American History\"}],\"name\":[{\"label\":\"Cast after\",\"content\":\"Leonard Wells Volk, 1828 - 1895\"},{\"label\":\"Sitter\",\"content\":\"Abraham Lincoln, 12 Feb 1809 - 15 Apr 1865\"}],\"topic\":[{\"label\":\"Topic\",\"content\":\"Mask\\\\Life mask\"},{\"label\":\"Topic\",\"content\":\"Abraham Lincoln: Male\"},{\"label\":\"Topic\",\"content\":\"Abraham Lincoln: Law and Law Enforcement\\\\Lawyer\"},{\"label\":\"Topic\",\"content\":\"Abraham Lincoln: Military\\\\Soldier\"},{\"label\":\"Topic\",\"content\":\"Abraham Lincoln: Politics and Government\\\\President of US\"},{\"label\":\"Topic\",\"content\":\"Abraham Lincoln: Society and Social Change\\\\Reformer\\\\Environmentalist\"},{\"label\":\"Topic\",\"content\":\"Abraham Lincoln: Business and Finance\\\\Businessperson\\\\Merchant\"},{\"label\":\"Topic\",\"content\":\"Abraham Lincoln: Politics and Government\\\\US Congressman\\\\Illinois\"},{\"label\":\"Topic\",\"content\":\"Abraham Lincoln: Politics and Government\\\\Government Official\\\\Surveyor\"},{\"label\":\"Topic\",\"content\":\"Abraham Lincoln: Politics and Government\\\\State Senator\\\\Illinois\"},{\"label\":\"Topic\",\"content\":\"Abraham Lincoln: Politics and Government\\\\Government Official\\\\Postmaster\"},{\"label\":\"Topic\",\"content\":\"Abraham Lincoln: Crafts and Trades\\\\Boat builder\"},{\"label\":\"Topic\",\"content\":\"Portrait\"}],\"physicalDescription\":[{\"label\":\"Medium\",\"content\":\"Plaster\"},{\"label\":\"Dimensions\",\"content\